      <h1 id="configuring-sriov-rdma-cni" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring an RDMA subsystem for SR-IOV<a href="#configuring-sriov-rdma-cni" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Remote Direct Memory Access (RDMA) allows direct memory access between two systems without involving the operating system of either system. You can configure an RDMA Container Network Interface (CNI) on Single Root I/O Virtualization (SR-IOV) to enable high-performance, low-latency communication between containers. When you combine RDMA with SR-IOV, you provide a mechanism to expose hardware counters of Mellanox Ethernet devices for use inside  Data Plane Development Kit (DPDK)    applications.</p>
      <h2 id="nw-sriov-configuring-sriov-rdma-cni_configuring-sriov-rdma-cni" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configuring SR-IOV RDMA CNI<a href="#nw-sriov-configuring-sriov-rdma-cni_configuring-sriov-rdma-cni" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Configure an RDMA CNI on SR-IOV.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>This procedure applies only to Mellanox devices.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You have access to the cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> role.</li>
      <li>You have installed the SR-IOV Network Operator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create an <code>SriovNetworkPoolConfig</code> CR and save it as <code>sriov-nw-pool.yaml</code>, as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1\nkind: SriovNetworkPoolConfig\nmetadata:\n  name: worker\n  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator\nspec:\n  maxUnavailable: 1 \n  nodeSelector:\n    matchLabels:\n      node-role.kubernetes.io/worker: \"\"\n  rdmaMode: <rdma_mode>"} lang="yaml" title="Example SriovNetworkPoolConfig CR" />
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.rdmaMode</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the RDMA network namespace mode. Set to <code>exclusive</code>.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>SriovNetworkPoolConfig</code> resource by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f sriov-nw-pool.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create an <code>SriovNetworkNodePolicy</code> CR and save it as <code>sriov-node-policy.yaml</code>, as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1\nkind: SriovNetworkNodePolicy\nmetadata:\n  name: sriov-nic-pf1\n  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator\nspec:\n  deviceType: netdevice\n  isRdma: <is_rdma>\n  nicSelector:\n    pfNames: [\"ens3f0np0\"]\n  nodeSelector:\n    node-role.kubernetes.io/worker: \"\"\n  numVfs: 4\n  priority: 99\n  resourceName: sriov_nic_pf1"} lang="yaml" title="Example SriovNetworkNodePolicy CR" />
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.isRdma</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies whether to activate RDMA mode. Set to <code>true</code>.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>SriovNetworkNodePolicy</code> resource by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f sriov-node-policy.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create an <code>SriovNetwork</code> CR and save it as <code>sriov-network.yaml</code>, as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1\nkind: SriovNetwork\nmetadata:\n  name: sriov-nic-pf1\n  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator\nspec:\n  networkNamespace: sriov-tests\n  resourceName: sriov_nic_pf1\n    ipam: |- \n  metaPlugins: |\n    {\n      \"type\": \"<plugin_type>\"\n    }"} lang="yaml" title="Example SriovNetwork CR" />
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>spec.metaPlugins.type</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies the type of meta plugin. Set to <code>rdma</code> to create the RDMA plugin.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>SriovNetwork</code> resource by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f sriov-network.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create a  <code>Pod</code> CR and save it as <code>sriov-test-pod.yaml</code>, as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: sample-pod\n  annotations:\n    k8s.v1.cni.cncf.io/networks: |-\n      [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"net1\",\n          \"mac\": \"20:04:0f:f1:88:01\",\n          \"ips\": [\"192.168.10.1/24\", \"2001::1/64\"]\n        }\n      ]\nspec:\n  containers:\n  - name: sample-container\n    image: <image>\n    imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent\n    command: [\"sleep\", \"infinity\"]"} lang="yaml" title="Example runtime configuration" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the test pod by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f sriov-test-pod.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Log in to the test pod by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc rsh testpod1 -n sriov-tests"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Verify that the path to the <code>hw-counters</code> directory exists by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ ls /sys/bus/pci/devices/${PCIDEVICE_OPENSHIFT_IO_SRIOV_NIC_PF1}/infiniband/*/ports/1/hw_counters/"} lang="terminal" />
